\subsection{Three-attachment bridges and four-attachment bridges with one interior vertex}
\label{dis:three-construction}

Suppose now that some path $P_i$ is not an edge and every bridge
with four attachments has one interior vertex. By
Proposition~\ref{dis:types}, every bridge with at least two
interior vertices then has three attachments. The next corollary of
Corollary~\ref{dis:lone-bridge} and Lemma~\ref{dis:aligned-contraction}
shows that these bridges have planar relevant completions. This
allows us to use the bridge forms from Section~\ref{sec:core} and combine
them in the enumeration~\supp{E5} to obtain the remaining graphs.

